# CITATION.cff
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Swage in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Swage: turning variable-sized dense segments into efficient GPU tile tasks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Abhik
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhiksark/swage"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Swage is an experimental Python-embedded MLIR/LLVM GPU compiler. It
  explores whether one segment-local program can support different fixed
  GPU work shapes as runtime segment lengths change. In the current
  pre-alpha release, the only public execution subset is a fixed vector-add
  kernel, lowered through MLIR and LLVM NVPTX for NVIDIA GPUs, and segmented
  sum, max, and ragged softmax run only as private qualification. After
  that release, two calls made a fixed segmented sum, max, and softmax
  public. Public segment syntax is planned.
